+A client plugin that merges **consecutive same-tool calls in the Web chat flow into one
+card with compact child rows**. It shadows the shipped `read`/`grep`/`glob`/`edit`/`write`/
+`bash`/`pwsh`/`web_search`/`web_fetch`/`run_code` toolviews in the web UI's
+`tool.call.toolview` slot (`priority: -1`) and, for each group, renders the merged main
+card on the group's first call while the remaining in-group calls render `null`. The host
+half declares the config row and registers it as the composition layer of the plugin's own
+`merge-tool-calls` settings namespace.
+
+Cohort: migrated from the 0.1.1-era client-runtime surface to **dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2**.
+
+## Documented capabilities and entry points
+
+1. **Keyed toolview shadowing.** The plugin takes over a wire tool's card by registering a
+   keyed `tool.call.toolview` entry for that tool name at `priority: -1` (ascending
+   shadowing rank; the lowest rank renders). Every claimed key replaces the shipped row;
+   unclaimed keys keep the shipped row.
+2. **Merged run detection.** Consecutive same-name calls merge into one group; known
+   families merge across names (`grep`+`glob`, `bash`+`pwsh`, `read`+`web_fetch`,
+   `write`+`edit`); an unknown tool merges only with itself. Any other node kind breaks
+   the run. `maxGroupSize` caps a group and the overflowing call starts its own group.
+3. **Merged main card.** The group's first call renders a main card whose summary is the
+   group count in the family's noun (`Read · 5 Files`, `Search · 3 Queries`,
+   `Bash · 4 Commands`, …), falling back to the first error line when the group's first
+   call failed. State (running / ok / error / interrupted) colours the row.
+4. **Compact child rows.** Every call in the group — including the first — is reachable as
+   a compact child row; the child block collapses by default and animates open from the
+   main row.
+5. **Bundle-row config through the settings seam.** `cordis.patch.yml` carries the
+   user-facing config: `tools` (`[]` = all built-in generic-row tools, or an explicit
+   whitelist of any wire name), `groupBy` (`adjacent`, or `step` for one group per agent
+   step), `maxGroupSize` (default 8). The host half validates the row with its exported
+   Schemastery `Config` and registers it as the `base` layer of the plugin's own
+   `merge-tool-calls` settings namespace; a `merge-tool-calls:` user section layers over
+   the row, and the browser half reads the resolved section through the client settings
+   scope, so a deployment's row values and a user's overrides both reach the merged rows.
+6. **Row copy in two shipped locales** (`zh`/`en`) through the client locale registry,
+   plus `ja`/`ko` language packs: the plugin registers the language definition
+   (`ctx.locale.addLanguage`) and its namespace dictionaries per locale
+   (`ctx.locale.register(NS, id, dict)`), so another pack that already defines the same
+   language keeps its own definition.
+7. **Pure presentation.** The merge is a pure function of the chat snapshot: no session
+   log, model-visible data, or details panel is touched; replay is deterministic.
+
+## Migration mapping (0.1.1-era → 0.1.2-alpha.2)
+
+| Old surface | Current surface |
+| --- | --- |
+| `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime/client` (client context + chat node types) | removed; `Context` from `@deepseek-ai/cordis` plus each owning package's type-only import |
+| `ctx.session` chat slice / `useSession(session => session.nodes)` | framework `useChat` hook on the session-scoped slot: `snapshot.order` + `snapshot.nodes.get(key)` |
+| `block.callView` / `block.resultView` | removed from the wire; card props derive from raw `argsRaw`/content/error |
+| `conversationContextKey(kind, id)` value import | not a public export; the row locates its own node by scanning `order` and matching `data.root.callId` |
+| `ctx.betterLocale` override service | shipped client locale registry language packs: `ctx.locale.addLanguage` + `ctx.locale.register(NS, id, dict)` (duplicate ids and duplicate `(ns, locale)` pairs now fail loudly) |
+| row config read only by the host half | the row is the `base` layer of the `merge-tool-calls` settings namespace; the browser half reads the resolved section through `ctx.settingsScope` |
+
+The grouping model and the register shape are exercised by
+`node --test` against the real source with React/primitive stubs (registration keys,
+`priority: -1`, family grouping, cap behaviour, card model, selector equality).
 
